Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Tier=202=20=C2=B7=20four=20evidence-flow=20refi?=
 =?UTF-8?q?nements=20(S1=20filters=20+=20S2=20strike=20hierarchy=20+=20S3?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20two-path=20request=20+=20S4=20DIO=20routing)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

S1 · Search/sort/filter on remaining evidence pages
  evidence-notams.html · new NOTAM Category filter (Runway / Taxiway /
    ILS-Nav / Airspace / Fuel-Ground / Other) with auto-classification
    from NOTAM text, plus a Sort control (Most recent / Severity /
    Airport). Airport counts on left rail reflect current category
    filter. Category chip appears on each NOTAM card.
  evidence-ash.html · simple search input over the Smithsonian volcanic
    activity side panel. Page remains in onboarding state pending VAAC
    QVA feed access.

S2 · Industrial Action storage restructured into country -> date -> event
  evidence-strikes.html · replaces flat DGAC/ENAC notice list with a
  hierarchical accordion: country header (France / Italy) -> date group
  -> event card. Each event holds four sub-categories of supporting
  documents: news articles, airport publications, internal emails,
  affected flights. Click event to expand and see all attached docs.
  Seeded with 4 realistic events (SNCTA nationwide ATC, CGT baggage,
  ENAV 24h ATC, USB ground-handling). Existing search + country filter
  continue to work.

S3 · Two-path evidence-request modal in module4-evidence-workspace
  Modal now opens with two tabs at the top:
    - Quick · pull from catalogue — tick-box list of 16 pre-existing
      catalogue items (METAR, SIGMET, NOTAM, ATFM, CRCO, ops log,
      commander report, crew records, Article 9, third-party rerouting,
      strike notice, news, wildfire, VAAC, flight track). Tick items
      -> DefendAble checks the case Evidence Repository and either
      pulls from repo or raises a targeted request per item.
    - Freeform · specific document — the original recipient/SLA/note
      form for cases where the solicitor knows the exact doc they need.
  Quick tab is default. Submit button label swaps based on active tab
  ('Pull selected from repo' vs 'Raise request').

S4 · Evidence-request routing aligned with DIO jurisdiction
  New 'DIO for this territory (auto-routed)' recipient added as the
  default option in the Freeform tab. On submit, pushNotification fires
  to the correct DIO id (england-wales -> EH, france -> FD, spain -> SR)
  based on the case's jurisdiction field, with the case ref, requestId,
  title + body, tab='requests' for deep-link routing.

Cache-bust: s12a across the four touched HTMLs.
